From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:03 2001
From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: initialize arrays used by duplicate checks

The duplicate filters in typec_switch_match() and typec_mux_match() read
all entries in the output arrays before fwnode_connection_find_matches()
has filled them. Zero-initialize both arrays so valid devices cannot be
dropped by comparisons against uninitialized stack contents.

Refreshed from armada's 0517-usb-typec-mux-dont-swallow-EPROBE_DEFER.patch
for cachyos-7.2.5-1. That base already returns -EPROBE_DEFER before both
duplicate checks when class_find_device() finds no device. Keep only the
array initialization that is still missing; retain the filename so the
handheld resolver substitutes this local copy in armada's series order.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux.c
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@
  */
 struct typec_switch *fwnode_typec_switch_get(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode)
 {
-	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS];
+	struct typec_switch_dev *sw_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS] = {};
 	struct typec_switch *sw;
 	int count;
 	int err;
@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@
  */
 struct typec_mux *fwnode_typec_mux_get(struct fwnode_handle *fwnode)
 {
-	struct typec_mux_dev *mux_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS];
+	struct typec_mux_dev *mux_devs[TYPEC_MUX_MAX_DEVS] = {};
 	struct typec_mux *mux;
 	int count;
 	int err;
